From: QEMU Anti-Detection Patches
Date: 2025
Subject: [PATCH] target/i386: Hide KVM hypervisor presence when expose_kvm is disabled

When the user sets "-cpu host,-kvm" (expose_kvm=false), hide all traces
of KVM hypervisor from the guest:

1. CPUID[1].ECX[31] (hypervisor bit) - don't set it when KVM is not exposed
2. CPUID[0x40000000].ECX[30] (KVM signature detection) - already handled
   by not injecting KVM leaves into KVM_SET_CPUID2

The EAC anti-cheat detection tool uses CPUID leaf 0x40000000.ECX[30] as
its primary trigger. This is part of the "KVMKVMKVM\0\0\0" signature
where ECX contains "VMKV". Bit 30 of this value is always 1 for KVM.

Without these patches, even with "-cpu host,-kvm", CPUID[1].ECX[31] still
advertises the hypervisor bit because it's unconditionally set in
x86_cpu_expand_features().

---
 target/i386/cpu.c | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/target/i386/cpu.c b/target/i386/cpu.c
index abcdef1..1234567 100644
--- a/target/i386/cpu.c
+++ b/target/i386/cpu.c
@@ -8406,7 +8406,9 @@
     /* legacy-cache defaults to 'off' if CPU model provides cache info */
     cpu->legacy_cache = !x86_cpu_get_versioned_cache_info(cpu, model);
 
-    env->features[FEAT_1_ECX] |= CPUID_EXT_HYPERVISOR;
+    if (kvm_enabled() && cpu->expose_kvm) {
+        env->features[FEAT_1_ECX] |= CPUID_EXT_HYPERVISOR;
+    }
 
     /* sysenter isn't supported in compatibility mode on AMD,
      * syscall isn't supported in compatibility mode on Intel.
@@ -9762,6 +9764,7 @@
 
     if (!kvm_enabled() || !cpu->expose_kvm) {
         env->features[FEAT_KVM] = 0;
+        env->features[FEAT_1_ECX] &= ~CPUID_EXT_HYPERVISOR;
     }
 
     /*
